<title>HONG KONG: Union Bank 1996 net rises 20.1 percent.</title>
<headline>Union Bank 1996 net rises 20.1 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   112.1  vs 95.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    30.0   vs 27.0</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items	nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    270.42 vs 225.14</p>
<p>    Company name		 Union Bank of Hong Kong Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  April 17-24</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   May 27</p>
<p>NOTE - Union Bank of Hong Kong provides banking, financial and investment services.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 40 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 10 cents) vs 36 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
